      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Cross Product of Two Vectors Whose Angle Is a Non-Special Angle",
      "problem": "The vector $u$ has magnitude $8$, the vector $v$ has magnitude $2,$ the angle between $u$ and $v$ is ${100}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $u\\times v.$ Find $u\\times v$ in terms of $n.$ Round your final answer to one decimal place where appropriate.",
      "worked_solution": "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|u|\\cdot |v|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =8\\cdot 2\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{100}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =16\\cdot (0.984\\,80…)\\cdot n \\\\  & =(15.756\\,92…)\\cdot n \\\\  & ≈15.8n.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
